WEBVTT

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.270
Kentaro!

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.470
Kentaro!

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.710
Have ya seen Kentaro?

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:52.560
No.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.410
If you see him, grab 'im.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.000
Mrs. Ichinose, what's the...?

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:01.880
What's she so mad about?

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.980
What's Kentaro done?

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.020
Who knows.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:22.730
Kentaro!

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:15.290
From next week, I'll be able
to go to your house again, Ikuko.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:16.690
Take it easy.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.720
I'll be okay.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.630
It won't be as fun.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.330
Say hello to your father.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:25.870
Get home safely.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:26.830
Okay!

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:27.740
Bye!

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:36.540
Uh... Would you like to
join me for dinner?

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:37.340
Huh?

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.950
I cooked enough for Ikuko.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:41.680
Sure.  I'd love to!

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.240
What's the matter?

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.390
-Sorry.
-It's okay.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:37.810
I know! You got
scolded by your mom?

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.280
She found the test
that I had hidden.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.840
She said I can't help it
if I did badly.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.970
But she's mad 'cause
I hid it from her.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.810
Well, that's life.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.450
You were crying
just because of that?

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:52.520
NO! I don't cry
about things like that!

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:54.720
I...

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:56.720
I have a secret.

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:57.590
What?

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.100
You gotta promise
you won't tell a soul!

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.100
I promise!

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.440
It's this.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:13.210
Ready?

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.150
TOKYO OLYMPICS

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:24.850
This?

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.190
It's Mr. Yotsuya from Room 4.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.450
He hasn't changed at all.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.960
How many years ago was
the Tokyo Olympics?

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:33.550
Do you know?

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:35.060
There's more.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:36.700
Look.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.230
Wow! A soldier!

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:41.900
Check him out!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:46.210
This can't be!

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.380
There's a scarier one.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.550
This.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.140
Maison Ikkoku
Grand Opening Ceremony.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.650
I've seen this photo before.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:05.160
This kid by the clock tower
is my grandpa when he was little.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.220
Look!

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.470
No way.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.250
I found it in the attic.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.890
No one could have done this!

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.510
But...

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.020
But this means Mr. Yotsuya is...

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.430
Is...

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:39.730
What?

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.690
He can't be.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:44.130
Just tell me!

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.400
I'll just get scolded again.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:34.000
Bathroom's so far!

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:38.350
I gotta go.
I can't hold it anymore.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:49.120
You know, he could be a vampire
or a time traveler...

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.890
or an immortal being.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.230
You saw it, didn't you?

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.110
The Specium Beam?

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:05.570
W-What the heck is that?

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.480
Can't you see this is a cross?!

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:16.620
That has no effect on me whatsoever!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.350
How about some tea?

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.590
No thanks.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:53.330
That Kentaro...

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:54.230
What?

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:56.930
Oh, never mind.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:01.370
Godai said Kentaro's
acting strange.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.300
Did something happen?

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:04.660
Godai said that?

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:10.310
I yelled at him the other day,
and he's been edgy ever since.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.780
I don't remember
raising him like that.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.050
Hello?  It's Otonashi.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.120
Hi Ikuko.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.690
Photos? What photos?

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.070
He found photos like that?

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:39.770
Mr. Yotsuya's
a strange one, all right...

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:40.810
but he can't be...

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.530
Do you know Mr. Yotsuya's first name?

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:46.150
I think he said the character
is written like "Kamekichi,"

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:47.770
but it's pronounced "Tsuruji."

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.050
He told me it's written like
"Fuji" but read "Kawadacho."

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.050
They're both lies.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.660
Come to think of it...

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:58.750
we really don't know anything
at all about Mr. Yotsuya.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.320
You're right.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.450
We just know he's a Peeping Tom.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:08.490
What're you two doin' here?

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:09.870
Nothing...

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:12.400
Let's go. Coach Mitaka
wants to talk to us.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:13.760
Coach?

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:19.180
That's right.
He can't be trusted.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:22.020
I've always had
a bad feeling about him.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:25.650
It's time we uncover
his true identity.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.080
U-Uncover? That's so harsh...

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.390
You're too lax! Now listen...

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.720
Why is Mitaka here?

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:34.030
Beats me.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:38.150
Hey, you two!
Now listen carefully.

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:40.810
Is this really necessary?

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:44.000
Would you like
to approach Yotsuya...

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.480
and ask for
an explanation, Godai?

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:48.810
You think he'll just
simply tell you?

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:51.410
N-No. I don't think so...

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:53.440
Right? You see?

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.380
But can't we be more subtle?

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:57.890
That's what I'm suggesting.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:10:59.860
We'll inconspicuously trail him...

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.220
and get some clues
about his general background.

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:05.690
Right, Ms. Otonashi?

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:06.630
Uh-huh.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:11.630
Count me out.
This ain't my cup o' tea.

00:11:12.010 --> 00:11:14.910
Fine. I can't force you.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.870
But don't leak this out to...

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:21.480
I know! I'll keep my mouth shut.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:22.850
Thank you.

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:26.380
So... Here's the plan.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:07.620
Deafening silence
It is the sound
of one hand clapping

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.590
It's a bit too quiet.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:27.940
Say...

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:31.580
Is Godai really up?

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:32.740
Well...

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:35.920
What time do you think
Mr. Yotsuya's gonna leave today?

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:37.250
Let's see...

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:40.560
He won't stay home today,
of all days, will he?

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.820
Why don't you calm down?

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:45.590
Me? I'm calm.

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:47.500
I'm gonna go wake up Godai.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:55.690
Good morning.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:57.740
Good morning.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:00.680
Well, I'll see you later.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:07.520
What'll we do?

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.210
We'll lose him.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:10.850
Shall we call it off for today?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:14.420
No way! Coach Mitaka's
standing by.

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.830
Well, then we better get Godai.

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:18.960
All right. You go.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:19.500
Sure.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:21.620
I'll go get Godai up.

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:23.200
W-What?

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:31.130
My goodness!

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:37.470
Why me?

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:42.580
I forgot something.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.190
Hurry!

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.050
Wait a second, Mrs. Ichinose!

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:10.990
Manager! Manager!

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:27.830
There they go!

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:52.460
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.960
Yotsuya's secret love child?!

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:03.230
C-Can't be!

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:05.640
Well, Sensei, bye!

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:08.530
Sensei?!

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:24.860
Hello?

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:26.570
Godai?

00:15:27.430 --> 00:15:30.290
Yes. The bus stop at Clock Hill?

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.330
I'll call Coach Mitaka right away.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:14.200
Well, if it isn't Young Godai.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:20.570
I was just thinking about
going to the Pachinko Parlor.

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.410
It's so lonely by myself.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:24.210
I believe fate has brought
us together here.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:26.050
Won't you join me?

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:27.680
S-Sure.

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.910
You'll buy me some balls,
will you not?

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:34.080
Godai screwed up.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:35.590
Mitaka was thrown off.

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:36.850
You're up next.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:38.320
Uh...

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:45.300
Um... Must I...really go like this?

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.130
Why not? It's YOU!

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:52.140
You look just like I did
when I was young!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:05.320
"International Relief Foundation
Far East Division"?

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:13.590
Hello? Coach Mitaka?
I heard what happened.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:17.190
Rendezvous with the manager
pronto. She's at...

00:18:58.370 --> 00:19:00.530
Sorry you had to see me like this.

00:19:00.610 --> 00:19:02.570
No, it's quite charming.

00:19:03.110 --> 00:19:04.900
Oh please!

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:06.390
Get down!

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.220
Where do you think he's going?

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:14.470
This time, I'll follow him.

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:19.050
You go to that building
and ask about him, please.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:20.850
Good luck.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:22.760
Don't take it so seriously.

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:09.640
What a coincidence!

00:20:09.710 --> 00:20:11.830
What brings you
to this part of town?

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:14.040
I'm out for a walk.

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:15.450
Why are you here?

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:19.110
Me? I'm on my way back from work.

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:22.980
Work? What line
of work are you in?

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:25.150
Since you ask...

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:35.000
You're a rubber band salesperson?

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:40.630
He who's addressed as "Sensei"
is not always a teacher.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:45.370
He who frequents an office is
not necessarily its employee.

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:50.180
The Chin Dynasty Emperor
built the Great Wall...

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.910
but wasn't a construction worker.

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:57.680
A man with a supply of rubber bands
may be a census taker.

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:02.320
People are
not always what they seem.

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:05.450
Oops! I better get going.

00:21:09.810 --> 00:21:11.300
Oh, by the way...

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:15.260
I need a 12-letter word...

00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:21.410
that means "close watch kept
over someone, as by a detective"?

00:21:21.920 --> 00:21:23.080
Any ideas?

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:28.470
You! You knew
everything, Yotsuya!

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:31.950
Gotcha!

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:37.690
Coach Mitaka's plan
failed miserably.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:41.690
Aren't there any photos
that'd give us clues?

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:44.800
They could have been
composite photographs.

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:47.100
I wouldn't be surprised
if Yotsuya made those up.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:50.540
But we have the grand opening
photos at our house, too.

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:54.170
Grandpa said he knows
nothing about Mr. Yotsuya.

00:21:57.990 --> 00:22:00.890
"Taken at Asakusa
International Theater."

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:03.380
"Subway Line Grand Opening."

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:07.930
"Japan-Germany
Anti-Communist Agreement."

00:22:09.360 --> 00:22:11.520
"Felix the Cat comes to town"...?

00:22:31.550 --> 00:22:32.770
Family album?!

00:22:33.090 --> 00:22:37.750
Yeah. He told me it's
a long-lost family album.

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:41.050
His uncle.

00:22:44.170 --> 00:22:45.220
His father.

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:49.730
And this is...

00:22:50.270 --> 00:22:52.390
His grandfather?

00:22:53.740 --> 00:22:55.570
Yup. He said the history
of Maison Ikkoku...

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:57.500
is his family history.

00:22:57.580 --> 00:22:58.270
See ya!

00:23:11.330 --> 00:23:12.490
Defense.

00:23:49.590 --> 00:23:52.110
Godai said he has finals.

00:23:52.190 --> 00:23:54.520
It's no use cramming now.

00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:58.360
Why do we have to stop
having our parties?

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:03.030
Next: "Big, Shocking Announcement?!
Kyoko Confesses Love to Godai"

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:04.960
You're kidding, right?

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:06.260
Yeah.
